 "lines": {
  "hook": "The cable just snapped. You're dropping down the shaft.",
  "b1": "You plan to jump. But your best jump is about seven miles an hour.",
  "b2": "From one hundred sixty five feet, you hit at seventy two miles an hour.",
  "b3": "Jump perfectly. Guess your new speed.",
  "b4": "Sixty five. Barely better, and you can't time it.",
  "b5": "Back up the shaft. Elevators hang on several steel ropes.",
  "b6": "Plus automatic brakes built to stop a fall.",
  "b7": "Betty Lou Oliver fell seventy five floors in the Empire State Building.",
  "b8": "Trapped air and coiled cables cushioned her. She broke her back, but lived.",
  "end": "When the cable snaps, forget the jump. Remember Betty."
 },
